Well, it's taken some 25 years, but now it's done. Gelrath the
Gnomish Wizard ascended on the Germany devnull tournament server.
Now I can scratch one item from the TODO list after being introduced
to Nethack (well, Hack anyway) way back in 1985. How come it's taken
this long? Well, first of all, I obviously haven't been playing
non-stop :-) There have been some periods of abstension lasting
for years during this time.

Also, I really am too impatient and careless for this game. I'll
build a good character every now and again that promptly experiences
a YASD. Often because I don't bother to stop and consider my options.

This time it was different. On entering the tournament I decided that
if I managed to get a character to the point where it should be
ascendable, I'd do it. I started playing random characters, but then
I got a gnomish wizard that I felt was a good bet. I normally don't
like playing wizards all that much, so I figured that I'd be forced
to think and not just play mindlessly. Also, being gnomish meant
an easier trip to mine town and a chance for a co-aligned altar.

I really became determined to make it when I managed to throw away
a really great opportunity to ascend one of my wizards. Late one
night (early one morning) I decided to stop playing, so I saved.
Just after doing so, I came to think of something that I really
should make certain had been done so I wouldn't forget (I can't
even remember what it was), so I thought "Well, just log on again,
fix that and then quit for today." And that's what I did. Including
the quit part. Not save. #quit. Curtains.

It wasn't all that long before I got another wizard going, and I
decided this would be the one. I played much slower and more
carefully than ever before. The game was pretty standard, but a
few highlights (and lowlights):

+ Found two magic lamps in the mines. One of them yielded a wish
(SDSM).
+ Sokoband gave a BoH.
- Got teleportitis before TC, and managed to jump into a pool when I
was
  a bit too fast in typing and didn't notice that I was teleported into
  a muddy room. Lost a whole bunch of spell books and scrolls.
+ Got a genocide scroll just after having had a run-in with an
Arch-Lich.
  Genocided L's. A while later, a second one turned up and took care of
h's.
  The last one (I think used for true genociding dispatched) ;'s, as a
  retribution for what they did to an earlier promising character on
  the medusa level.
+ Medusa level was the Titan version, and I quickly found myself in
  trouble. Dug down, returned up and took out Medusa and after that
  the Titan without much trouble.
+ Castle wand at (0:2), first wish used on a magic marker.
- Wasted a scroll of charging (my last) by chosing the wrong MM to
charge.
- Decided to wish for PYEC, since I thought I only had seen two
artifacts
  (MB and the Eye). I failed to get it, and later found that I had been
  given Fire Brand at a much earlier stage, stashed it and forgotten
it...
- With a WoW at (0:0) and no charging, I decided first to polypile (at
Ludios)
  I normally don't bother with polypiling, but this game I was going to
win
  at all costs. It didn't get me any charging, though.
+ Set up a camp at an altar since I had the CM spell. After a while a
  black pudding was created, so I took that as a hint from the RNG to
do
  something else I normally don't do. A few hundred puddings later one
dropped
  a scroll of charging. By this time, I was crowned, had a naked AC of
-1,
  HP:s in the 300's and most of the stuff that I had needed to charge
the
  wand for...
+ Had an uneventful trip down through Gehennom, bribing the bribable
ones.
+ I dispatched of Rodney with +FoD both the first time, and then
whenever
  he cared to show up. The sanctum was also cleared mostly using +FoD
with
  no problems.
+ The force was with me, only sent me downwards a handful of times.
+ Took my time equiping myself for the endgame at my stash on dlvl 1.
  This time, I would think of everything!
+ Earth was quickly dug through, travelling with jumping.
- I arrived at air, donned Levitation Boots... Or rather, would have
  if I hadn't forgotten them in the stash. No ring, spell or potions
  either. Had to propel myself by kicking monsters, throwing /WoDig
  no longer needed, etc. When I was knee-deep in monsters summoned by
an
  Archon, I started to wonder whether I'd actually make it. Although I
  never was really low on HP, needing free space in order to move was
  problematic. Luckily for me I had more than a few /WoT to clear the
  way with, and I finally managed to kick myself into the portal.
+ Fire was a breeze.
+ Water also.
+ Arrived on astral and was given a companion. Not that it did me any
  good, I left my Archon far behind me when jumping toward the altar.
  Left was closest, and had Pestilence. Blinded him with my camera,
  but he still made me ill, so he got a dose of /WoDeath. Another on
  the way back, since the altar was chaotic.
+ Next, middle altar with Famine. Once I had a snapshot of Famine, he
  never bothered me again. The altar, however, was lawful.
+ OK, so to the right, and Death. Death didn't like to have his
  picture taken either, so I never had to take him on. Plowed my way
  to the altar, charmed everything around me to get some company on
  the way out and...

- ...started the cut and pasting, but managed to paste the first screen
  contents back into the window, so every character on the screen was
  taken as a command... Oops. Many .'s there... Luckily enough there
  were no rothes standing to the right of a sink, followed by a yellow
  light :-) It did give the priests some opportunity to summon a few
  insects, though... After (more than) a few nervous space key presses,
  all was still OK. Phew, new attempt:

